{
    "_comment": "(12.11) SECRET ENDING: the Void beaten with all 3 lore items given away. WHITE, silence until line 8, there ending_secret starts (assets/music/ending_secret.mp3); after the last line the music fades, a short silence, then the credits.",
    "partner": "narrator",
    "backdrop": "white",
    "auto": true,
    "music": "silence",
    "pictures": {
        "name": "secret",
        "from_line": 8
    },
    "start": "monologue",
    "nodes": {
        "monologue": {
            "lines": [
                {
                    "id": "ending_extra_01",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "...",
                    "skippable": true,
                    "speed": 0.08
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_01",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "You listened."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_02",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "To a voice on a tape. To a broken light. To a few old words. All of them, to the end."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_03",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Do you know how rare that is? Most people stop at the part they like."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_04",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Down here, everything that was cut away was waiting for one thing. Not to win. Not to be destroyed."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_05",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Just to be looked at, by someone who wouldn't look away."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_06",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "And you didn't."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_07",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "So it isn't hiding anymore. It's coming home.",
                    "do": {
                        "music": "ending_secret"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_08",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Not all at once. That was always the fear. A little at a time, the way rain comes back after a long summer."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_09",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "The world will have sad days again. Somebody will lose something. Somebody will say the wrong thing at dinner."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_10",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "And somebody else will stay, and listen, and say it's alright."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_11",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "That was the part they forgot, when they built it. You can't have one without the other."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_12",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "A world with nothing bad in it isn't a kind world. It's a photograph of one."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_13",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "The pale place under everything is fading. There is nothing left for it to hold."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_14",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "The one who stood guard can finally rest. He was so tired of being brave."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_15",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Healing isn't making the dark go away. It's letting it back in, and finding there's room."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_16",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "So keep a little room for it. In the world. In yourself."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_17",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Thank you, for listening to the end."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_18",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Now go on. Somebody up there is waking up, and the sky is a little less perfect today. It suits it."
                },
                {
                    "id": "ending_secret_19",
                    "who": "narrator",
                    "text": "Good morning.",
                    "hold": 330
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}
